\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Here, Lord, we offer Thee 
\par all that is fairest,
\par Bloom from the garden, and 
\par flowers from the field,
\par Gifts for the stricken ones, 
\par knowing Thou carest
\par More for the love than the 
\par wealth that we yield.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. send, Lord, by these to the 
\par sick and the dying;
\par Speak to their hearts with
\par a message of peace;
\par Comfort the sad, who in 
\par weakness are lying;
\par Grant the departing a 
\par gentle release.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Raise, Lord, to health again those 
\par who have sickened,
\par Fair be their lives 
\par as the roses in bloom;
\par Give of Thy grace to the souls 
\par Thou hast quickened,
\par Gladness for sorrow, and 
\par brightness for gloom.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

